From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:01:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): Free parks a model that can park, and a full
 device answers RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0022-server-park-when-told.patch), with the backend's side here.

A model that takes context on demand, on a device whose weight buffers can
leave it and come back (SYCL with GGML_SYCL_PARKABLE=1), no longer has to
be stopped to give its device memory back. With LocalAI's own two calls,
and no new one:

- Free PARKS it: the context is freed, the weights are copied to host
  memory and leave the device; the process, its tokenizer and everything
  validated at the load stay. The answer is success with the message
  "parked" and, in metadata, {"parked":true,"park_size":<bytes>,"ms":..}.
- LoadModel for the model the process already holds brings the weights
  back, then answers what it always answered, byte for byte: "Model
  already loaded". Not parked, it is the no-op it was.
- a request to a parked model brings the weights back by itself.
- Status says where the weights are: memory.total is their bytes held in
  host memory now, the breakdown "parked", "park_size", "parks", "unparks".

A model that cannot park answers Free and Status with Unimplemented, as
this backend always did: the caller stops the process, and samples it, as
before. Free while a request runs answers FailedPrecondition "busy" - it
is for now, where Unimplemented is for good - and the model stays on the
device.

One status for "the device has no room now". When parked weights cannot
come back, when a context cannot be created, or when the device refuses
memory in the middle of a graph, the request - Predict, PredictStream,
Embedding, Rerank, TTS, Score, the slot cache, a decision - and a repeated
LoadModel are answered RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED, where they were INTERNAL like a
fault. Nothing is wrong with the request or the model; the model stays as
it was (parked, if it was), and the same request can be sent again. Not
UNAVAILABLE, which LocalAI reads as a backend it can no longer reach.
Every other error is INTERNAL, as before.

The messages and the codes are in park_reply.h, tested without a model
(park_reply_test.cpp): a proxy in front of a backend tells a return from a
load by the bytes of "Model already loaded". prepare.sh probes the
checkout (LOCALAI_HAS_PARK), so a fork without the llama.cpp patch builds
this file as before, Free and Status unimplemented.

Checked without a device, on a CPU build of this backend with a stand-in
for a device that parks and refuses (a dev patch, in no build): 29 of 29
over gRPC - a model that cannot park answers as before; Free, Status and
LoadModel as above; the first vectors bit for bit over 12 cycles, returned
by LoadModel and by the request; a refused return is RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED
with the model still parked and the next request served; 302 calls of Free
beside live requests, each done or refused busy, every request's vectors
intact. NOT run: any of it on a device, or through LocalAI's server, which
today calls Free only before it stops a process.

